# Line endings.
#
# The Linux package ships shell scripts and freedesktop/systemd files that are
# parsed by programs which do NOT tolerate CRLF: /bin/sh reports
# "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M" and refuses to run, systemd and polkit silently
# mis-parse the trailing carriage return into the value. Development happens on
# Windows, where Git's autocrlf would otherwise hand these files CRLF endings, so
# pin them explicitly rather than relying on a contributor's local config.

* text=auto

*.sh            text eol=lf
*.service       text eol=lf
*.desktop       text eol=lf
*.policy        text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf

# Batch files are the mirror image: cmd.exe needs CRLF.
*.bat           text eol=crlf

# Binaries and pre-hashed payloads must never be touched. The sing-box engine is
# checked against a SHA256 pin; any normalisation would break that verification.
*.exe           binary
*.dll           binary
*.so            binary
*.ico           binary
*.png           binary
*.pem           text eol=lf
